<title>THAILAND: THAI RICE VESSELS LOADING AND MOVEMENTS AT AUG. 7.</title>
<headline>THAI RICE VESSELS LOADING AND MOVEMENTS AT AUG. 7.</headline>
<dateline>BANGKOK 1997-08-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Thai Commerce Ministry and independent surveyors detailed rice loading at Thai ports as follows (in tonnes):</p>
<p>Vessel		Date of Arrival   Quantity     Destination</p>
<p>SUN SEA		 16/07/97	   10,600	  Africa</p>
<p>BANG YERUA	    16/07/97	    5,500	  Brunei</p>
<p>BANG LUANG	    16/07/97	    5,700	  Malaysia</p>
<p>ANDREY LAVROV	 18/07/97	   12,000	  Nigeria</p>
<p>ELIROPEAN	     18/07/97	    6,000	  Nigeria</p>
<p>KUM GANG		23/07/97		400	  Vietnam</p>
<p>DOU MEN		 23/07/97	    1,100	  China</p>
<p>SANGTHAI CHENESE    25/07/97	     --	    HK</p>
<p>SANGTHAI FORTUNE    25/07/97	    2,352	  Singapore</p>
<p>BANG KHUNTIEN	 25/07/97	    5,500	  Malaysia</p>
<p>DIBENA UNITY	  25/07/97	    7,200	  Malaysia</p>
<p>SOON SING	     25/07/97	    2,000	  India</p>
<p>BONNY		   25/07/97	   10,000	  Africa</p>
<p>PRADU		   28/07/97	    4,400	  Malaysia</p>
<p>NEBULA		  28/07/97	    1,500	  Riji Island</p>
<p>CAPPITAL QUEEN	29/07/97	    5,000	  Japan</p>
<p>-- Bangkok newsroom (662) 652-0642</p>
</text>
